# Legado File Size Policy

**Only this repository (`legado`) opts out of the global 300-line code-file split rule.**

- Prefer editing existing files in place even when they exceed 300 lines.
- Do not refactor/split solely to satisfy a line-count limit.
- Split only when it clearly improves ownership, reuse, or the user asks for it.

## How the exception works

Real exemption is the repo-local hook override:

- `.cursor/audit-hooks/custom_rules.json` — disables `edit_target_too_long` / `write_too_large` / `file_too_long*` for this workspace only.

This `.mdc` is agent guidance only; it does **not** replace the hook override.

Repos without both the hook override and this marker still enforce the global 300-line limit. Other repos are unaffected.
